## Constraints (hard)

1. **UdpCap preferred** for DNS residual (UDP query path) — winner class almost certainly lives here.
2. **NetCap residual only** where hard raw/L2 — do **not** re-label DNS as NetCap residual.
3. **`dns_server.oo` phantom honesty** — batch_2 five-file claim is **not tree-backed**; do not create the file to retro-greenwash.
4. **No real UDP DNS crypto as product** — no resolver, no DoH/DoT product, no DNSSEC evaluate path in this residual close.
5. **Smoke shapes** — pass + fail fixtures (immune axiom); check allow/deny, not marketing.
6. **No product code from Fairy** — this file is Decide input only.

## Darwin 1.11 scorecard

Score each idea **0–10** (higher = survives compile cycle). Axes (sum /5 ≈ Darwin rank):

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Cap** | Matches preferred granular (UdpCap) / keeps hard NetCap only for raw |
| **Honest** | Residual named; no crypto/product greenwash; batch_2 phantom not reanimated |
| **Smoke** | Cheap pass+fail shapes; hooks existing cap_g1 / cap_g6 rails |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S = U+F+W+O\) (untested claims, fail-open, hand-waves, oversize) |
| **Ship** | ≤ one small file + smoke; line pressure; orthogonal to DE emit inject |

**Rule:** loser ideas pruned (do not implement). Winner only advances to DE1.

